WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.612
A common beginner mistake is writing equals NULL
That does not test

00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:08.388
whether a value is missing It asks whether a known
value is

00:00:08.412 --> 00:00:12.950
equal to an unknown value and SQL cannot prove the
comparison The

00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:17.162
result is UNKNOWN even for rows where the column is
NULL The

00:00:17.175 --> 00:00:22.825
same issue affects not-equal NULL SQL provides
explicit missing-value predicates

00:00:23.062 --> 00:00:27.438
IS NULL and IS NOT NULL Run the example and inspect
the

00:00:27.462 --> 00:00:32.263
calculated columns You should see NULL results
instead of useful true or

00:00:32.288 --> 00:00:36.525
false answers When the question is whether a value
is missing use

00:00:36.538 --> 00:00:40.225
IS NULL Treat that as a basic SQL habit
